TODO

* the animation subsystem is Clay's transitions (see "Animation" in
  docs/vue-graphics-stack.md): the button highlights and the tool panels
  use it; popup windows (menus) cannot, they are separate SDL windows
* the printer dialog offers the options lpoptions reports (paper size,
  two-sided, color); orientation would need a rotation of the PDF
* the debug view (F1) shows the element tree; its own scroll bars and
  toggles are Clay's and are not styled like ours
* the colour picker offers named colours only; the bg flag, the patterns
  and the background images of the Qt picker are not implemented. The
  colour menus do not reach it at all: they route on (qt-gui?) and fall
  back to the Scheme rgb picker, which is richer, so this is not urgent
* the wheel always scrolls the view: wheel-capture? is not asked, so the
  wheel does not pan a graphic (edit_graphics.cpp calls graphics-wheel for
  it), and control-wheel does not zoom as it does in the Qt port
* resize_widget ignores the initial scrolling position (hpos, vpos), and
  user_canvas_widget ignores its style
* no image previsualizer in the file chooser (the native dialog has none)
* copying a selection as an image to the clipboard is Qt-only
  (graphics_file_to_clipboard); the menu entry is hidden
* the tree view does not observe its tree, so a database browser will not
  refresh by itself (Qt has QTMTreeModel)
* responsive tabs are plain tabs: the "gui:responsive tab mode" preference
  does nothing
* Windows: perform_select and the pipe layer are stubs, so no plugins and
  no client/server there; printing shells out to CUPS
* Linux: no X11 PRIMARY selection (SDL has only the system clipboard), and
  the interface is drawn in the TeX fonts rather than a desktop UI font

